{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ee33f172f47041dd","name":"The Infinite Empire","source":{"id":"source:reference-ee33f172f47041dd","title":"The Infinite Empire","revision":22436,"timestamp":"2024-09-03T21:49:36Z","sha256":"7800ff1c00295ff28a911fb259a936f998a973cf151aa4f19460a83ea8a8b290","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22436","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Infinite%20Empire&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ee33f172f47041dd","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rakata"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakata","referenceId":"reference:0b233b768a3d506b"}," are an ancient Species, whose society once stretched from ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Unknown Regions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Unknown_Regions"}," to distant parts of the galaxy, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Corellia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Corellia","referenceId":"reference:b23d752dcc50dee4"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manaan","referenceId":"reference:e148d0a9b917e831"},". They called it The Infinite Empire. At the height of their civilization, they built a massive space station factory called ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Star Forge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Star_Forge"}," that enabled them to create the machinery and ships needed to manage their massive, interstellar empire. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," powered their technology, and they relied on their connection to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," to control it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Their natural Force-sensitivity (perhaps even their predisposition toward ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},") allows them to make machines that operate in the same way. Rakatan Force-drives give power to Skipships that hopscotch between worlds rich in life, leading to an empire with a spotty, patchwork appearance. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rakata"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakata","referenceId":"reference:0b233b768a3d506b"}," enslave all they find and alter the ecosystems of worlds such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vagar Praxut"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vagar_Praxut?action=edit&redlink=1"},". By 30,000 BBY, The Infinite Empire reaches its height, stripping bare such planets as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Duro"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Duro","referenceId":"reference:649f085c70b1304a"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Morseer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Morseer?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and forcing the Coruscantis and Corellians to build weapons of colossal scale. Rakatan forces defeat the era's other major powers, including the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gree?action=edit&redlink=1"}," and the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kwa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kwa?action=edit&redlink=1"},", and only the double blow of a plague and a civil war weakens their hold sufficiently to permit a slave revolt in 25,200 BBY.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For unknown reasons, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rakata"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakata","referenceId":"reference:0b233b768a3d506b"}," eventually lost their ability to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". As their grasp over the machinery and technology weakened, so did their control over their subjugated worlds. The native ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," managed to throw off their masters and regain control of their own destinies. However, the impact of Rakatan technology would be felt by some of these worlds for thousands of years to come.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Infinite Empire Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rakatan Guardian Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakatan_Guardian_Droid","referenceId":"reference:345351b473f57339"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rakatan Guardian Droid Squad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakatan_Guardian_Droid_Squad","referenceId":"reference:cb3447a0a61c9324"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 7\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Battalions"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Rakatan Guardian Droid Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rakatan_Guardian_Droid_Battalion","referenceId":"reference:c846f68654422411"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 11\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"br","children":[]},"\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
